@fm description | description | The seasonal baking plan and special loaves of Crumbwick Bakery.
# Seasonal baking
s description | Crumbwick bakes four seasonal loaves each year: spring dill, summer fig, autumn oat and winter spice.
s description | Seasonal loaves go on level two beside the pinnock loaves.
## Winter spice loaf
s rule{sea_spice} | Bake the winter spice loaf in the big oven only.
s gate | Do not add the spice mix until the dough has risen once.
s gate{sea_rise} | Let the dough rise once before you add the spice mix.
s example | For example, a spice mix added at the start made the dough sticky and the crumb grey.
s description | The spice mix has cinnamon, clove and a pinch of orrel seed.
## Summer fig loaf
l rule | Soak the figs in warm water for ten minutes
l rule | Dry the figs on a clean cloth
l prohibition{sea_figs} | Do not add wet figs to the dough
l description | Figs come in a box of sixty and arrive on Thursday
l example | A fig loaf with wet figs split along the top in the oven
## Orders for the season
s rule | Take Christmas orders from the first of November.
s gate{sea_plan} | Check the oven plan for the week before you accept a big Christmas order.
s prohibition{sea_nolate} | Never accept a Christmas order after the twentieth of December.
s description | The oven plan hangs on the wall of the dough loft.
s example | Case: a late order for sixty winter spice loaves took the whole oven for a night and the daily bread came late.
## Decorations
s rule | Hang the paper stars in the window on the first of December.
s prohibition | Do not tape anything to the glass of the oven door.
s none | The shop looks lovely in the snow.
